   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the education law, in relation to allowing retirees of the New\nYork state teachers' retirement system who suspend their retirement the option\nof a benefit recalculation after two years of service",
    "basePrintNo": "S9296",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9296-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §503, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9296\n\nSPONSOR: RYAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to allowing retirees of\nthe New York state teachers' retirement system who suspend their retire-\nment the option of a benefit recalculation after two years of service\n\n \nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\n\nThis bill amends Education Law Section 503(11) to allow retired members\nof the New York State Teachers' Retirement System (NYSTRS) to suspend\ntheir retirement, return to work and have the option of a benefit recal-\nculation after working at least two years of additional service.\n\n \nSUMMARY AND JUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnder NYSTRS current statute, Education Law Section 503(11)(b), retirees\nare permitted to suspend their retirement and return to work to have\ntheir benefit recalculated after five years or upon re-retiring with at\nleast two years of service, they become eligible to receive two separate\nretirement benefits. In order to avail the retiree of the recalculation\nafter five years of additional service, the member is required to pay\nback all the pension benefits received under the original retirement\nbenefit, with interest, or take an actuarial equivalent lifetime\nreduction.\n\nThe System proposes an amendment to Education Law Section 503(11) to\nmirror the provisions of Retirement and Social Security Law Section 101\navailable to members of the New York State and Local Employees' Retire-\nment System (NYSLRS). Under Retirement and Social Security Law Section\n101, NYSLRS members may avail themselves of a recalculation after two\nyears of member service credit after restoration to active service and\nonly if such member returns to the retirement system with regular inter-\nest the actuarial equivalent of the amount of the retirement allowance\nreceived in the first retirement or repayment through actuarial\nreduction.\n\nIn addition, the System recognizes that allowing retirees the option of\nrecalculating their benefit after two years of service, instead of five\nyears, may assist those who believe they attained a service credit mark-\ner, but after verification with the school district employer the service\nrecord is adjusted. For example, in some cases, members retiring believe\nthey have reached their intended service credit milestone, twenty years,\nbut once the service has been verified with the employer the service\ncredit is less than what was anticipated. At that point, it could be\nvery difficult for the retiree to return to the position they retired\nfrom or even find a similar position. Additionally, it may take time to\nfind any employment after they have retired. Reducing the benefit recal-\nculation requirement to two years, could make it easier for the retiree\nto avail themselves of the recalculation already provided in law at five\nyears and may provide employers an opportunity to hire an experienced\nworker to fill in during a transition and assist in succession planning.\n\nThe amendments proposed in this bill would amend the provisions govern-\ning NYSTRS retirees (Education law Section 503) to allow retirees to\nsuspend their retirement, return to work and have the option of either a\nbenefit recalculation or a separate benefit after two years of service.\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE OF THE BILL:\n\nThis act shall take effect June 30, 2022 and apply to all members of\nNYSTRS, except that if this act shall have become a law on or after June\n30, 2022, this act shall take effect immediately, shall be deemed to\nhave been in full force and effect on and after June 30, 2022.\n\n \nOTHER AGENCIES TO WHOM THE BILL MAY BE OF INTEREST:\n\nDivision of the Budget, Department of Financial Services.\n\n \nBUDGETARY IMPLICATIONS OF THE BILL:\n\nIf this bill is enacted, the annual cost to the employers of members of\nthe New York State Teachers' Retirement System is estimated to be negli-\ngible.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
